<title>DENMARK: Codan 96 pre-tax profit 968 mln DKK.</title>
<headline>Codan 96 pre-tax profit 968 mln DKK.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>12 months to December 31 1996</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Group pre-tax result	     968    vs 741</p>
<p> Net result after minorities    1,071  vs 561</p>
<p>Insurance result(Danish/Swedish</p>
<p> accident/life			  941  vs 707</p>
<p> Gross premiums, total	    6,145  vs 5,796</p>
<p> Own capital end-1996	     5,941  vs 5,023 end-1995</p>
<p> Proposed dividend (percent)     22.5  vs 20.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Denmark's second biggest insurer is A/S Forsikringsselskabet Codan, 71.45 percent owned by Britain's Royal &amp; Sun Alliance. It said in a statement that it expected 1997 results similar to those of 1996. --Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom, 45-33-969650</p>
</text>
